{title: Blessed Be Your Name (FJ_35_en)}
{song_number: 35}
{language: en}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[A]Blessed be Your [E]name in the [F#m7]land that is plentiful, [E]
where Your [F#m7]streams of abundance [E]flow. Blessed [D]be Your name.
[A]Blessed be Your [E]name when I'm [F#m7]found in the desert [E]place,
though I [F#m7]walk through the wilder[E]ness. Blessed [D]be Your name.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Vorrefrain}
[A]Every blessing [E]You pour out I'll [F#m7]turn back to [D]praise.
[A]And when the darkness [E]closes in, Lord, [F#m7]still I will [D]say:
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[D]Blessed be the [A]name of the Lord, [E]blessed be Your name.
[F#m7]Blessed be the [D]name of the [A]Lord, [E]blessed be Your
glo[F#m]ri[E]ous [D]name.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[A]Blessed be Your [E]name when the [F#m7]sun's shining down on [E]me,
when the [F#m7]world's all as it should [E]be. Blessed [D]be Your name.
[A]Blessed be Your [E]name on the [F#m7]road marked with suffer[E]ing,
though there's [F#m7]pain in the offer[E]ing. Blessed [D]be Your name.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Vorrefrain}
[A]Every blessing [E]You pour out I'll [F#m7]turn back to [D]praise.
[A]And when the darkness [E]closes in, Lord, [F#m7]still I will [D]say:
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[D]Blessed be the [A]name of the Lord, [E]blessed be Your name.
[F#m7]Blessed be the [D]name of the [A]Lord, [E]blessed be Your
glo[F#m]ri[E]ous [D]name.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
[E]You give and take away, You give and take away.
My [D6]heart will choose to [A]say: Lord, [E]blessed be Your [D]name.
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus}
[D]Blessed be the [A]name of the Lord, [E]blessed be Your name.
[F#m7]Blessed be the [D]name of the [A]Lord, [E]blessed be Your
glo[F#m]ri[E]ous [D]name.
{end_of_chorus}
